  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ocean conference CI Liberia - CI Ocean conference Liberia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Oceankonferens CI Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Ambassaden har f&#xE5;tt en f&#xF6;rfr&#xE5;gan fr&#xE5;n Conservation International att finansiera projektet &quot;Blue Ocean Conference&quot; med SEK 3,318,525 kr. Konferensen planeras genomf&#xF6;ras 18&#x2013;22 mars, 2019. 

Konferensen syftar till att f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra hanteringen och nyttjandet av havet utanf&#xF6;r Liberia genom att &#xF6;ka medvetenheten hos akt&#xF6;rer som fiskare, konsumenter och beslutsfattare kring m&#xE4;nniskans p&#xE5;verkan p&#xE5; haven genom att arbeta med b&#xE5;de nationella och internationella akt&#xF6;rer f&#xF6;r att 
st&#xE4;rka en h&#xE5;llbar utveckling och f&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra hanteringen av marinresurser. 

Conservation international kommer vara huvudansvarig f&#xF6;r att genomf&#xF6;ra konferensen tillsammans med den Liberianska regeringen och s&#xE4;rskilt Liberian Marine Authority (LiMA), Liberian Enviromental Protection Agency (EPA) och National Fisheries, Aquaculture Authority of Liberia (NaFAA). Niras och den svenska ambassaden i Monrovia deltar i utformandet av konferensen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation International has applied to the Embassy of Sweden in Monrovia for funding of 3,318,525 SEK to carry out the &quot;Blue Ocean Conference&quot; in Liberia during the period March 18-22, 2019. 

The intervention aims at improving the management and use of oceans in Liberia by raising awareness of stakeholders such as fishermen, consumers and decision-makers on the issues impacting seas and oceans and to work across disciplines, both with national and international actors, to discuss possible actions that can be taken to improve management and sustainable development of marine resources. 

Conservation International will implement the conference together with the Liberian Government&#x2019;s agencies such as the Liberian Maritime Authority (LiMA), the Liberian Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) and the National Fisheries and Aquaculture Authority of Liberia (NaFAA).  Niras and the Embassy of Sweden i Monrovia will be part of the planning of the conference.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of conference was to raise awareness of the threats facing Liberia&#x2019;s marine ecosystem and economy as well as identifying innovative solutions which allow for a long-term sustainability. The aim was for the conference to serve as turning point for ocean work not only in Liberia but also more broadly across the continent of Africa, being a long neglected area in spite of the large population being heavily dependent on services stemming from the ocean.</narrative>
  </description>
